# Linear Algebra Exercises 📐

Hands-on NumPy exercises covering core linear algebra concepts for machine learning — vectors, cosine similarity, projections, linear classifiers, and dimensionality.

Each exercise includes the problem statement, a worked-out written solution, and Python (NumPy) code with results and visualizations.

## 📒 Notebook

- [LinearAlgebra\_Binal.ipynb](./LinearAlgebra_Binal.ipynb)

## 📚 Exercises Covered

| # | Exercise | Concepts |

|---|----------|----------|

| 1 | Vector Treasure Hunt | Vector addition, magnitude (norm), unit vectors |

| 2 | Movie Match-Maker | Cosine similarity, recommendation logic |

| 3 | Are You On My Side? | Signed distance, half-space classification |

| 4 | Shadow Puppets | Vector projection, perpendicular components |

| 5 | Build a 2-Line Classifier | Linear decision boundaries, manual classification |

| 6 | Curse-Breaker Investigation | High-dimensional distance behavior, normalization |

| 7 | Draw Your Own Galaxy | Rotation matrices, correlated data generation |

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

- Python 3

- NumPy

- Matplotlib

## 🚀 Running the Notebook

1. Clone this repo:

```bash

git clone https://github.com/yourusername/linear-algebra-binal.git

```

2. Install dependencies:

```bash

pip install numpy matplotlib

```

3. Open LinearAlgebra\_Binal.ipynb in Jupyter Notebook, JupyterLab, or Google Colab and run all cells.

